exports[`brief generator > renders a basket of capabilities without repeating the rules 1`] = `
"# bb plugin: 2 capabilities

Goal: build one bb plugin that provides the capabilities below.
Verified against bb desktop-v0.43.3 (commit e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0), @get-bb/plugin-sdk 0.4.104.
The SDK installed on this machine is the contract: run \`bb plugin types\`, then read
node_modules/@get-bb/plugin-sdk/bundled-types/bb-plugin-sdk-app.d.ts (frontend) or bb-plugin-sdk.d.ts (backend)
before writing code. If a symbol below is missing there, the installed bb is older or newer — trust the declarations, not this brief.

## Scaffold
\`\`\`
bb plugin new <name>      # creates ./bb-plugin-<name> — no flags; scaffold has server.ts, app.tsx, skills/
cd bb-plugin-<name>
bb plugin install .       # registers the directory in place
bb plugin dev             # rebuild + reload on every save
\`\`\`
Manifest entries needed for these capabilities: \`bb.app\`, \`bb.server\`

## Architecture
app.tsx (useRpc) → bb.rpc → server.ts → storage/network. State lives on the server; the frontend, the CLI and the agent are three clients of one \`server.ts\`.

## Capabilities
### 1. Home-screen sections (\`homepage-section\`) — \`app.slots.homepageSection({ id, title, component })\`
Adds a full-width section to the page bb opens on, below the prompt box. With this, a plugin can:
- Render its own component across the width of the content area
- Render before any thread exists, which suits shortcuts and pinned work
- Render after bb's own content, in the order plugins registered
- Manifest entry: \`bb.app\`
- Props/handler type: \`PluginHomepageSectionProps\`
- Slot kind: additive — several plugins coexist in this slot
- Stability: stable
- \`PluginHomepageSectionRegistration\` — packages/plugin-sdk/src/app-contract.ts:504

### 2. bb CLI commands (\`cli\`) — \`bb.cli.register(defineCli({ name, summary, commands }))\`
Registers a top-level \`bb <name>\` command, available in the terminal and to agents. With this, a plugin can:
- Be invoked the same way by a person at a terminal and by an agent mid-task
- Receive the thread and project it was invoked from, when bb knows them
- Make the plugin usable from scripts and automations, not only from the UI
- Declare commands, arguments and options once and get parsing, \`--help\`, nearest-name suggestions and JSON errors
- Manifest entry: \`bb.server\`
- Props/handler type: \`PluginCliRegistration\`
- Slot kind: additive — several plugins coexist in this slot
- Stability: stable
- \`PluginCli\` — packages/plugin-sdk/src/backend-contract.ts:1033
- \`PluginCliResult\` — packages/plugin-sdk/src/backend-contract.ts:980
- \`defineCli\` — packages/plugin-sdk/src/cli-spec.ts:1174
- \`cliCommand\` — packages/plugin-sdk/src/cli-spec.ts:252
- \`PluginCliError\` — packages/plugin-sdk/src/cli-spec.ts:230
- \`PluginCliSpec\` — packages/plugin-sdk/src/cli-spec.ts:211
- \`PluginCliCommand\` — packages/plugin-sdk/src/cli-spec.ts:189
- \`PluginCliOption\` — packages/plugin-sdk/src/cli-spec.ts:99
- Read \`plugins/concurrency-limit/server.ts\` — defineCli + cliCommand with typed options and PluginCliError with a hint.
- Read \`plugins/tasks/cli/index.ts\` — Grouped command paths such as "project create".

## Rules that will bite you
- The frontend has no network plane of its own. Call your server entry through \`useRpc\` → \`bb.rpc\`; never \`fetch\` from \`app.tsx\`.
- \`experimental_Diff\` takes the host's shared highlight worker pool from React context: thread and nav panels have one, homepage and settings sections do not, so code there renders unhighlighted.
- Your styles are scoped to \`:where([data-bb-plugin=<id>],[data-bb-plugin-root]:not([data-bb-plugin]))\`. Only default-theme Tailwind utilities are emitted; custom \`@theme\` colors and hand-written \`oklch(...)\` literals will not survive the build.
- Each slot is wrapped in its own error boundary. A crash shows a chip and the rest of bb keeps working — but the crash is sticky for the session, so fix it rather than relying on the fallback.
- The CLI handler runs inside the server process, not in the CLI: \`argv\` excludes the command name and \`ctx.signal\` aborts when the invoking request disconnects.
- \`PLUGIN_CLI_OUTPUT_MAX_BYTES\` is 1 MiB of stdout + stderr combined, and the host rejects an oversized result atomically instead of clipping it.
- Core bb commands always win a name collision; your plugin stays reachable as \`bb plugin run <id>\`. Use \`defineCli\` so \`--help\`, unknown-flag hints and \`--json\` envelopes come for free.
- Plugins are full-trust code inside the server process: they can read all local bb data, including other plugins' secrets. \`secret: true\` settings are plaintext files with mode 0600, not encrypted. Design accordingly.

## Done when
1. \`bb plugin build\` completes without errors
2. \`bb plugin install .\` then \`bb plugin dev\` loads the plugin — \`bb plugin list\` shows it \`running\`
3. Your section renders full width under the new-thread prompt box, after bb's own content
4. projectId === null (no project selected) renders something sensible rather than throwing
5. Disabling the plugin (\`bb plugin disable <id>\`) returns bb to its previous behaviour with no leftovers
6. bb <name> --help renders without executing plugin code and bb <name> <command> returns your exit code
7. Output stays under PLUGIN_CLI_OUTPUT_MAX_BYTES; the host rejects an oversized result atomically

## Source of truth
- Home-screen sections: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-api-map/src/surfaces.ts#L485
- bb CLI commands: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-api-map/src/surfaces.ts#L621
- \`PluginHomepageSectionRegistration\`: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-sdk/src/app-contract.ts#L504
- \`PluginCli\`: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-sdk/src/backend-contract.ts#L1033
- \`PluginCliResult\`: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-sdk/src/backend-contract.ts#L980
- \`defineCli\`: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-sdk/src/cli-spec.ts#L1174
- \`cliCommand\`: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-sdk/src/cli-spec.ts#L252
- \`PluginCliError\`: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-sdk/src/cli-spec.ts#L230
- \`PluginCliSpec\`: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-sdk/src/cli-spec.ts#L211
- \`PluginCliCommand\`: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-sdk/src/cli-spec.ts#L189
- \`PluginCliOption\`: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-sdk/src/cli-spec.ts#L99
"
`;

exports[`brief generator > renders a headless namespace 1`] = `
"# bb plugin API namespace: bb.storage (\`storage\`)

Goal: implement this capability in a bb plugin.
Verified against bb desktop-v0.43.3 (commit e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0), @get-bb/plugin-sdk 0.4.104.
The SDK installed on this machine is the contract: run \`bb plugin types\`, then read
node_modules/@get-bb/plugin-sdk/bundled-types/bb-plugin-sdk-app.d.ts (frontend) or bb-plugin-sdk.d.ts (backend)
before writing code. If a symbol below is missing there, the installed bb is older or newer — trust the declarations, not this brief.

## What it does
Stores the plugin's data on the bb server. With this, a plugin can:

## Where it plugs in
- Manifest entry: \`bb.server\` (backend)
- Registration: \`bb.storage.kv.* · bb.storage.database() · bb.storage.migrate(db, statements)\`
- Stability: stable

## SDK symbols
- \`PluginStorage\` — packages/plugin-sdk/src/backend-contract.ts:179

## Read this first
- \`plugins/memory/server.ts\` — Owns a SQLite schema through migrate() and queries it directly.
- \`plugins/side-chat/server.ts\` — Uses namespaced kv with a prefix sweep instead of a database.

Clone or open the bb repo at that commit to read them.

## Rules that will bite you
- \`bb.storage.kv\` values are JSON capped at 256 KB each; anything bigger or relational belongs in \`bb.storage.database()\`.
- Migrations are append-only by index: the host records each statement's hash and rejects a changed or reused index.
- Storage isolation is a convention of the \`bb.storage\` helpers, not an enforced boundary — another plugin can open your \`data.db\` with ordinary \`fs\`.
- The factory is time-boxed at 30 s and its return value is discarded. Register cleanup with \`bb.onDispose\` (LIFO) — services, schedules, listeners, content scripts, everything.

## Done when
1. \`bb plugin build\` completes without errors
2. \`bb plugin install .\` then \`bb plugin dev\` loads the plugin — \`bb plugin list\` shows it \`running\`
3. Data survives reload and restart
4. A second migration appends a statement instead of editing an applied one
5. Disabling the plugin (\`bb plugin disable <id>\`) returns bb to its previous behaviour with no leftovers

## Source of truth
- \`PluginStorage\`: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-sdk/src/backend-contract.ts#L179
- bb's own Plugin Guide: enable the \`plugin-api-docs\` plugin, then open Plugin Guide
- Pinned upstream tree: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-sdk/src
"
`;

