exports[`brief generator > renders an experimental exclusive slot 1`] = `
"# bb plugin surface: The thread list (\`thread-list\`)

Goal: implement this capability in a bb plugin.
Verified against bb desktop-v0.43.3 (commit e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0), @get-bb/plugin-sdk 0.4.104.
The SDK installed on this machine is the contract: run \`bb plugin types\`, then read
node_modules/@get-bb/plugin-sdk/bundled-types/bb-plugin-sdk-app.d.ts (frontend) or bb-plugin-sdk.d.ts (backend)
before writing code. If a symbol below is missing there, the installed bb is older or newer — trust the declarations, not this brief.

## What it does
Replaces the list of threads in bb's sidebar with a component your plugin renders. With this, a plugin can:
- Render every row, and decide the grouping, the ordering, and what each row shows
- Read the same live thread data and run statuses bb's own list reads
- Replace only the list. The New thread button, the search action, the plugin rows, and the sidebar footer stay bb's

## Where it plugs in
- Manifest entry: \`bb.app\` (frontend bundle)
- Registration: \`app.slots.experimental_threadList({ id, title, description, component })\`
- Props/handler type: \`PluginThreadListProps\`
- Slot kind: exclusive — one plugin owns this per installation and the user picks the winner in Settings → Appearance, so do not assume yours is active
- Stability: experimental — the name carries an \`experimental_\` prefix and both the name and the shape can change in a minor release; see docs/api_to_audit.md

## SDK symbols
- \`PluginThreadListRegistration\` — packages/plugin-sdk/src/app-contract.ts:1181
- \`PluginSidebarThreadsState\` — packages/plugin-sdk/src/app-contract.ts:991

## Read this first
- \`examples/plugins/replacement-lab-alpha/app.tsx\` — Shows conditional delegation to Original, the deliberate crash path and how two plugins contend for the same area.

Clone or open the bb repo at that commit to read them.

## Rules that will bite you
- Only one plugin can own this at a time; the user picks the winner in Settings → Appearance. Do not assume yours is active.
- bb passes \`Original\`. Render it to delegate — that is the supported way to handle the cases you do not want to own.
- The frontend has no network plane of its own. Call your server entry through \`useRpc\` → \`bb.rpc\`; never \`fetch\` from \`app.tsx\`.
- Row anchors must carry \`data-sidebar-thread-shortcut-target=""\` and \`data-sidebar-thread-id={thread.id}\`, or bb's \`thread.next\` / \`thread.previous\` shortcuts silently stop working.
- Each slot is wrapped in its own error boundary. A crash shows a chip and the rest of bb keeps working — but the crash is sticky for the session, so fix it rather than relying on the fallback.
- Every \`experimental_\` member is in \`docs/api_to_audit.md\` and gets renamed project-wide when it stabilizes. Compatibility aliases warn for one release and then throw.

## Done when
1. \`bb plugin build\` completes without errors
2. \`bb plugin install .\` then \`bb plugin dev\` loads the plugin — \`bb plugin list\` shows it \`running\`
3. Settings → Appearance → Sidebar lets the user pin your list, and the sidebar scroll area renders it
4. Rows carry data-sidebar-thread-shortcut-target and data-sidebar-thread-id so thread.next / thread.previous keep working
5. Disabling the plugin (\`bb plugin disable <id>\`) returns bb to its previous behaviour with no leftovers

## Source of truth
- Surface definition: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-api-map/src/surfaces.ts#L101
- \`PluginThreadListRegistration\`: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-sdk/src/app-contract.ts#L1181
- \`PluginSidebarThreadsState\`: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-sdk/src/app-contract.ts#L991
- bb's own Plugin Guide: enable the \`plugin-api-docs\` plugin, then open Plugin Guide → The bb app window → 4
- Pinned upstream tree: https://github.com/get-bb/bb/blob/e865697f56bea89f3413dd4cc7fae964850d20a0/packages/plugin-sdk/src
"
`;
